From 0ec3e7f18cdd043327bd13311f704d9e7726e871 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Jean-Micha=C3=ABl=20Celerier?=
 <jeanmichael.celerier@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 12:23:13 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] SPIRV-Cross: convert gl_ViewID_OVR to int for ViewIndex

SPIR-V's ViewIndex builtin is a signed int; GL_OVR_multiview2 declares
gl_ViewID_OVR as "in highp uint". The GLSL backend substituted the name
with no conversion, so every use in an int context became an implicit
uint -> int conversion, which GLSL rejects:

  0(100) : error C7011: implicit cast from "uint" to "int"
      isf_ViewIndexVarying = gl_ViewID_OVR;

The builtin is read-only and builtin_to_glsl is its only reference in the
GLSL backend -- the emitter never declares it, since the extension does --
so folding the conversion into the returned name is safe.

Affects any multiview shader lowered to GL: the pipeline is never created
and nothing draws.
---
 src/3rdparty/SPIRV-Cross/spirv_glsl.cpp | 10 +++++++++-
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/3rdparty/SPIRV-Cross/spirv_glsl.cpp b/src/3rdparty/SPIRV-Cross/spirv_glsl.cpp
index f9b489c..6980370 100644
--- a/src/3rdparty/SPIRV-Cross/spirv_glsl.cpp
+++ b/src/3rdparty/SPIRV-Cross/spirv_glsl.cpp
@@ -10554,7 +10554,15 @@ string CompilerGLSL::builtin_to_glsl(BuiltIn builtin, StorageClass storage)
 		if (options.vulkan_semantics)
 			return "gl_ViewIndex";
 		else
-			return "gl_ViewID_OVR";
+			// SPIR-V's ViewIndex is a signed int, but GL_OVR_multiview2 declares
+			// gl_ViewID_OVR as "in highp uint". Substituting the name alone
+			// leaves an implicit uint -> int conversion at every use, which GLSL
+			// forbids, so a shader that assigns ViewIndex to an int fails to
+			// compile:
+			//   error C7011: implicit cast from "uint" to "int"
+			// This builtin is read-only and never declared by the emitter, so
+			// the conversion is safe to fold into the name.
+			return "int(gl_ViewID_OVR)";
 
 	case BuiltInNumSubgroups:
 		request_subgroup_feature(ShaderSubgroupSupportHelper::NumSubgroups);
-- 
